//    DESCRIPTION:
//  as/visual is library to draw things to the
//  terminal via ANSI manipulation.
//
//
//    USAGE:
//
//
//  struct position: {X Position, Y Position}.
//
//  boxDecor(int): Sets box lines to a preset.
//
//  draw(position): Moves the cursor to a
//  specified terminal location.
//
//  drawBox(position, position): Draws an outline
//  from two positions.
//
//  drawPoint(position, as::string): Prints a
//  string to a specified terminal location.
//
//  drawSquare(position, position, char): Draws a
//  rectangle from two positions, filled by a 
//  char.
//
//  drawSTR(position, string, string, int): Draws
//  a string (Second) at position (Bottom
//  Left), filled by a character (First), 
//  wrapping around at a specified X position.
//
//  resize(int, int): Prompts the user to resize
//  their terminal to an automated guide.
//
//  setBoxLine(string x6): Sets each line 
//  character to a custom value.
//    DESCRIPTION:
//
//  as/rawIO is a more advanced and intimate look
//  into the In / Out system in a terminal by 
//  using the likes of the stty raw function.
//
//
//    USAGE (MENU):
//
//
//  - First, define the options to be displayed
//  by the menu by using the as::option[#][#] 
//  variable.
//
//  Use it by stating the vertical position in
//  the first brackets, then, stating the
//  horizontal position in the second.
//
//  - Second, make note of any blank spots,
//  find the position through the formula of:
//  Row position + (Column Position) * Max # of Rows.
//
//  Note that Row position starts at 1, and
//  Column position at 0.
//
//  Then, take the position, put it into the
//  brackets of as::exclude[#], and set the 
//  variable equal to true.
//
//  - Third, find the top left position on the 
//  terminal you want the column of options to 
//  appear, set the brackets of as::pos[#], and 
//  set the value equal to the position struct
//  which is {X Position, Y Position}.
//
//  - Fourth, choose a highlight color (All 
//  defined under <as/standard>), set the 
//  variable as::highlight equal to it.
//
//  - Fifth, put the command 
//  as::menuInit(int, int) with the amount of 
//  rows and columns respectively.
//
//  - Sixth, make a while loop with the condition
//  of (as::ch != KEY_ENTER), and put any 
